["+/", -8.397945404052734]]}, {"t": "/", "lp": -0.0031232680194079876, "top": [["/", -0.0031232680194079876], ["/C", -6.145049095153809]]}, {"t": "C", "lp": -0.0010436256416141987, "top": [["C", -0.0010436256416141987], ["CPP", -7.865005016326904]]}, {"t": "++", "lp": -0.010733364149928093, "top": [["++", -0.010733364149928093], ["XX", -4.552181720733643]]}, {"t": " compiler", "lp": -0.0008871316676959395, "top": [[" compiler", -0.0008871316676959395], [" (", -8.464191436767578]]}, {"t": "\n\n", "lp": -0.2383997142314911, "top": [["\n\n", -0.2383997142314911], [" (", -1.8216898441314697]]}, {"t": "These", "lp": -0.023885486647486687, "top": [["These", -0.023885486647486687], ["Both", -5.034761428833008]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line, explaining each flag and its purpose.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag ensures it works even if already sourced. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` won't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nStops the build immediately if any command fails (exits non-zero). Essential for catching errors early.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S` : **source directory** (where the source code lives)\n- `-B` : **build directory** (where compilation output goes)\n- `-G Ninja` : Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, parallel-friendly alternative to Make)\n\n## Build Type & Installation\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with compiler optimizations enabled (`-O3`), no debug symbols.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install binaries to `/usr`\n- Install libraries to `/usr/lib` (important on multiarch systems)\n\n## The Compilers\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's compilers:\n- **`icx`** : Intel oneAPI DPC++/C compiler\n- **`icpx`** : Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ compiler\n\nThese"}